### Goal Model Decomposition

---

#### **Goal Tables**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1      | Deliver Food and Retrieve Dishes | Ensure food is delivered to inpatient rooms and dishes are retrieved from rooms. | -                  | Achieve   | -        | Main objective of the system. |
| G2      | Deliver Food               | Deliver meals from the kitchen to inpatient rooms on an order-by-order basis. | #                  | Achieve   | G1       | Delivery and retrieval are parallel tasks. |
| G3      | Retrieve Dishes            | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient rooms and return them to the kitchen. | #                  | Achieve   | G1       | Retrieval is a separate task from delivery. |
| G2.1    | Handle Food Delivery Order | Process a single food delivery request (navigate, pick up, deliver). | ;                  | Perform   | G2       | Each order is handled sequentially. |
| G2.2    | Determine Delivery Method  | Decide whether to place the meal on the table or have the patient fetch it. | FALLBACK(G2.2.1, G2.2.2) | Query     | G2.1     | Uncertainty in patient capability requires fallback. |
| G2.2.1  | Place Meal on Table        | Use robot's special manipulation skill to place the meal on the table. | -                  | Perform   | G2.2     | Default method if no cooperation is needed. |
| G2.2.2  | Fetch Meal from Tray       | Cooperate with inpatient, companion, nurse, or another robot to fetch the meal. | -                  | Perform   | G2.2     | Alternative if patient cannot fetch. |
| G2.3    | Track Meal Retrieval       | Log when and where each meal was retrieved by the inpatient. | -                  | Perform   | G2.1     | Required for accountability. |
| G2.4    | Alert Wrong Meal Retrieval | Notify if an inpatient retrieves the wrong meal. | -                  | Perform   | G2.1     | Ensures correct meal delivery. |
| G3.1    | Handle Dish Retrieval Order | Process a single dish retrieval request (navigate, retrieve, return). | ;                  | Perform   | G3       | Each retrieval is handled sequentially. |
| G3.2    | Determine Retrieval Method  | Decide whether to retrieve dishes unassisted, with another robot, or with a human. | FALLBACK(G3.2.1, G3.2.2) | Query     | G3.1     | Uncertainty in cooperation availability requires fallback. |
| G3.2.1  | Retrieve Dishes Unassisted | Use robot's manipulation skill to retrieve dishes from the room. | -                  | Perform   | G3.2     | Default method if no assistance is needed. |
| G3.2.2  | Retrieve Dishes with Assistance | Cooperate with another robot or human to retrieve dishes. | -                  | Perform   | G3.2     | Alternative if unassisted retrieval is not feasible. |
| G3.3    | Open Room Door             | Open the room door, possibly with cooperation from another robot or human. | FALLBACK(G3.3.1, G3.3.2) | Query     | G3.1     | Uncertainty in door access requires fallback. |
| G3.3.1  | Open Door Unassisted       | Use robot's door-opening capability to enter the room. | -                  | Perform   | G3.3     | Default method if no assistance is needed. |
| G3.3.2  | Open Door with Assistance  | Cooperate with another robot or human to open the door. | -                  | Perform   | G3.3     | Alternative if unassisted opening is not feasible. |

